# SECURITY (prettier foot-gun): PL/pgSQL files use single-token
# lines that the formatter line-wraps, breaking the syntax. The
# specific tokens at risk are 'END IF;' and 'END $$;' which must
# each stay on a single line for psql to parse the migration.
# This is the durable fix for the recurring corruption noted in
# commit 384cc05 ("fix(db): repair formatter-induced syntax
# breakage in 0021 migration") and again in the follow-ups. Once
# a SQL file is excluded here, prettier will not touch it.
database/**/*.sql
# Markdownlint has its own handbook (docs/architecture/SKILLS_MINDMAP.md
# section 9.5); exclude pre-commit hook artifacts.
.husky/_/*
